cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this chart, cite the source of its values as below."
type: dataset
title: "lookdev-24: the workspace's 24-patch color chart"
abstract: >
  Our own 6 by 4 layout of 24 flat patches, row-major from top-left, carrying
  published colorimetric values: the BabelColor Avg. (spectral average of 20
  charts) sRGB 8-bit, L*a*b* D50 and xyY D50 figures from Pascale (2006),
  Table 2. chart24.json holds the values and chart24.svg draws them; both are
  copies of entities-sakuragaoka-station's tools/calib files. The cyan patch's
  R' = 0 is clipped in sRGB.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: "1"
date-released: 2026-10-01
commit: 74eb6b1a7827ffcc401265b7ae0eb6af0c30faba
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/contract-orbit-views"
url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-fire"
keywords:
  - color-chart
  - colorimetry
  - calibration
references:
  - type: report
    title: "RGB coordinates of the Macbeth ColorChecker"
    authors:
      - family-names: Pascale
        given-names: Danny
    publisher:
      name: "The BabelColor Company"
    date-published: 2006-06-01
    url: "https://babelcolor.com/index_htm_files/RGB%20Coordinates%20of%20the%20Macbeth%20ColorChecker.pdf"
    notes: "Table 2 (8-bit), the BabelColor Avg. block, gives srgb8, lab_d50 and xyY_d50; the manufacturer's 2005 block gives the check_* columns."
  - type: software
    title: "entities-sakuragaoka-station: tools/calib/chart24.json and chart24.svg"
    authors:
      - name: "V-Sekai-fire"
    commit: 74eb6b1a7827ffcc401265b7ae0eb6af0c30faba
    url: "https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/entities-sakuragaoka-station"
    notes: "Independent check: chart24-krita-check.json, 24 of 24 patches exact in Krita 5.3.4."
